== 1.8 Chapter 1 Practice Drill — 40 Questions

40 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 44 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [Geography is best defined as the study of],
  [the rocks that make up the crust],
  [the capitals and products of countries],
  [the spatial relationships between the earth and its people],
  [the earth's surface features only]
)

#mcq(2, [The two main branches of geography are],
  [cartography and surveying],
  [regional and national geography],
  [geology and meteorology],
  [physical and human geography]
)

#mcq(3, [The branch of physical geography that studies landforms is],
  [biogeography],
  [hydrology],
  [climatology],
  [geomorphology]
)

#mcq(4, [Climatology is the study of],
  [the atmosphere and its long-term patterns],
  [the formation of soils],
  [the distribution of plants and animals],
  [the movement of people]
)

#mcq(5, [Which of the following is a topic in human geography?],
  [the formation of a delta],
  [the density of population in a region],
  [the weathering of granite],
  [the classification of clouds]
)

#mcq(6, [The zone of the earth in which all life exists is the],
  [biosphere],
  [hydrosphere],
  [lithosphere],
  [atmosphere]
)

#mcq(7, [Which of the following is NOT one of the four spheres studied in geography?],
  [lithosphere],
  [biosphere],
  [hydrosphere],
  [stratosphere]
)

#mcq(8, [A geographic information system is best described as],
  [a satellite that photographs the earth],
  [a map drawn to scale],
  [an instrument for measuring rainfall],
  [a computer system that stores and analyses layers of spatial data]
)

#mcq(9, [The collection of information about the earth's surface from aircraft or satellites is called],
  [surveying],
  [remote sensing],
  [fieldwork],
  [cartography]
)

#mcq(10, [The instrument used to measure rainfall is the],
  [hygrometer],
  [barometer],
  [rain gauge],
  [anemometer]
)

#mcq(11, [The study of the distribution, growth and movement of people is called],
  [political geography],
  [economic geography],
  [settlement geography],
  [population geography]
)

#mcq(12, [Economic geography is chiefly concerned with],
  [the study of landforms],
  [the location of production, trade and consumption],
  [the structure of the atmosphere],
  [the classification of soils]
)

#mcq(13, [Which statement correctly distinguishes weather from climate?],
  [Weather is the condition at a moment; climate is the long-term average],
  [They are the same thing],
  [Weather is the average condition; climate is the condition at a moment],
  [Climate changes hourly; weather changes yearly]
)

#mcq(14, [A sketch map differs from a scale map because a sketch map],
  [shows relief by contours],
  [is not drawn to a stated scale],
  [uses grid references],
  [always covers a whole country]
)

#mcq(15, [Cartography is the],
  [measurement of rainfall],
  [classification of rocks],
  [study of population],
  [study of maps and map making]
)

#mcq(16, [The first stage of a fieldwork exercise is],
  [measuring the last sample],
  [drawing the graph],
  [writing the conclusion],
  [defining the problem and planning the method]
)

#mcq(17, [Which of the following is a method rather than a branch of geography?],
  [biogeography],
  [climatology],
  [statistics],
  [population geography]
)

#mcq(18, [A geographer's unit of analysis is chiefly],
  [the spatial distribution of phenomena],
  [the historical document],
  [the chemical formula],
  [the individual mineral]
)

#mcq(19, [Which question is the most distinctively geographical?],
  [When did the war end?],
  [Why is industry concentrated in this town rather than that one?],
  [How does a battery work?],
  [What is granite made of?]
)

#mcq(20, [Geography is described as both a science and a social science because it],
  [avoids measurement],
  [studies natural processes and human behaviour together],
  [deals only with maps],
  [uses only laboratory experiments]
)

#mcq(21, [Hydrology is the study of],
  [the atmosphere],
  [the distribution of living things],
  [the formation of rocks],
  [water on and under the land]
)

#mcq(22, [Soil geography is chiefly concerned with],
  [the movement of people],
  [the formation, classification and distribution of soils],
  [the making of maps],
  [the study of clouds]
)

#mcq(23, [Biogeography studies],
  [the chemistry of rocks],
  [the growth of cities],
  [the movement of goods],
  [the distribution of plants and animals]
)

#mcq(24, [Settlement geography is the study of],
  [the origin of earthquakes],
  [the composition of the atmosphere],
  [where and how people live],
  [the classification of climates]
)

#mcq(25, [A geographer who calculates the mean rainfall of ten stations is using],
  [remote sensing],
  [fieldwork],
  [statistics],
  [cartography]
)

#mcq(26, [An aerial photograph differs from a topographic map mainly because a photograph],
  [shows only the coastline],
  [is always drawn to a larger scale],
  [cannot show relief],
  [shows the surface as it appears, without symbols or a grid]
)

#mcq(27, [In a GIS, a layer is],
  [the height of the land],
  [a map's scale],
  [a single set of spatial data, such as roads or rivers],
  [a sheet of tracing paper]
)

#mcq(28, [The main limitation of fieldwork is that],
  [it cannot use instruments],
  [it cannot measure anything],
  [it never produces original data],
  [a single visit records only one moment]
)

#mcq(29, [Which of the following is NOT a tool of the geographer?],
  [a telescope for studying stars],
  [a questionnaire],
  [a rain gauge],
  [a map]
)

#mcq(30, [The clearing of a forest changes runoff, soil and local temperature. This illustrates],
  [the separation of the four spheres],
  [the interaction of the four spheres],
  [the irrelevance of physical geography],
  [the end of the water cycle]
)

#mcq(31, [On a map with a scale of 1 : 25 000, 1 cm represents],
  [25 km],
  [2.5 km],
  [250 m],
  [25 m]
)

#mcq(32, [A map is best described as],
  [a list of place names],
  [a photograph of the earth],
  [a representation of part of the earth's surface on a plane, to scale],
  [a three-dimensional model]
)

#mcq(33, [The statement 'the study of the earth as the home of man' emphasises that geography],
  [studies the relationship between people and their environment],
  [is only about physical features],
  [deals only with maps],
  [is the same as geology]
)

#mcq(34, [Which of these is a practical use of geography in national planning?],
  [writing a constitution],
  [choosing a site for a dam from rainfall and relief data],
  [training a football team],
  [composing a song]
)

#mcq(35, [Satellite imagery is a product of],
  [statistics],
  [fieldwork],
  [remote sensing],
  [cartography]
)

#mcq(36, [Which pair correctly matches a branch with its subject?],
  [biogeography — population],
  [climatology — rocks],
  [hydrology — water],
  [geomorphology — climate]
)

#mcq(37, [The most reliable way to measure the discharge of a stream is],
  [to measure its cross-section and velocity],
  [to estimate it by eye],
  [to ask a farmer],
  [to photograph it]
)

#mcq(38, [The relationship between geography and other sciences is best described as],
  [total dependence on geology],
  [complete independence],
  [borrowing methods and findings while keeping a spatial focus],
  [a rivalry with no overlap]
)

#mcq(39, [A candidate who lists facts about a country without explaining their distribution has],
  [described rather than explained],
  [used a GIS],
  [answered a geographical question fully],
  [carried out fieldwork]
)

#mcq(40, [The chief advantage of a map over a photograph is that a map can show],
  [selected information such as relief, boundaries and land use],
  [the weather at the time],
  [only what the eye sees],
  [the scene in colour]
)

